id: pm-todos-il19
title: Isolate concurrent packed fixtures from repository merge-driver configuration
description: "Release PR #116 failed Node 22.18.0 coverage when npm 10 ran prepare during concurrent pack calls despite ignore-scripts, contending on Git config. Daily Release run 38043122621 then timed out on the failed required check. Preserve canonical prepare semantics and pack identical built artifacts without shared repository writes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T04:59:23.453Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T00:57:59.627Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T23:30:47.091Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T23:30:47.091Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Implemented and merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/117: concurrent packed fixtures are isolated from merge-driver Git config writes"
expected_result: "Delivered outcome: Isolate concurrent packed fixtures from repository merge-driver configuration."
actual_result: "Merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/117 with green required CI checks and a completed CodeRabbit full review with every finding resolved; concurrent packed fixtures are isolated from merge-driver Git config writes"
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T05:00:14.694Z",codex-agent,"CI run 38043303831 failed 1 of 301 tests: integration.test.ts packed the built package while npm ran prepare despite ignore-scripts; concurrent pack callers attempted pm merge install on the same Git config. Daily run 38043122621 passed its release gate but timed out waiting for this failed required check. Investigating a deterministic fixture boundary that preserves canonical prepare installation and package bytes."
  "2026-10-11T05:02:21.422Z",codex-agent,"Design: backport the artifact-time prepare boundary already merged in pm-ops PR #152. A small documented predicate skips pack/publish before the unchanged pinned installer; npm ci/install still execute canonical resolution and fail on broken installers. The canonical suffix remains byte-identical. Held-lock regressions cover both lifecycle commands and real npm pack while checking Git config, lock, manifest and payload bytes. No dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-11T05:05:31.410Z",codex-agent,"Behavior-only revert proof: replaced only isArtifactCreation with return false and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pack prepare preserves|publish prepare preserves\" test/prepare-merge-driver.test.ts. Exit 1: both modules/tests loaded, 0 passed and 2 assertion failures (installer status 5 instead of 0 while config lock was held). Restored the predicate; no template or test changes in the reversion. The original CI failure is a real pack prepare conflict, not an identity or coverage-threshold failure."
  "2026-10-11T05:07:46.188Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test run passed 11/11 with zero failures/skips in the default schema context. Automatic linked-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Follow-up pm-todos-7bk6 tracks the stale workflow-approval timeout diagnostic without changing the release workflow in this fix. After this fix merges, release PR #116 must be closed and regenerated from fixed main; its branch still lacks the guard and its failed release run produced no tag or publication."
  "2026-10-11T05:21:35.734Z",codex-agent,"Exact-floor real-pack proof: in a scratch copy of the unchanged source and regression test, using Node 22.18.0 / npm 10.9.3, changed only isArtifactCreation to return false. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real npm packing\" test/prepare-merge-driver.test.ts failed a loaded assertion (0 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped), reproducing npm prepare attempting Git config installation with its lock held. Restored only that predicate and repeated: 1 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; archived manifest/payload and config/lock bytes verified. Active full-gate source was not mutated during this proof."
  "2026-10-11T06:35:40.059Z",codex-agent,"Draft fix PR #117 is open at bb33acd on a separate fix branch. Release PR #116 remains unchanged at dd40ac5bc2c620e6bb1869b1e7a55e3598617c61 and must be closed and regenerated from fixed main after this fix merges. Full local npm and isolated-HOME Node 22.18.0/npm 10.9.3 release gates remain active at unchanged thresholds; Bun gate remains scheduled. Completed lifecycle and linked checks passed 11/11, and npm 10 real-pack function-only revert fails then restores successfully."
  "2026-10-11T07:00:22.350Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR #117 CI run 38118503344 passed Node 22.18.0 and Node 26 at 304/304 with zero failures/skips; Node 26 full release also passed canonical-reader 1/1 and packed acceptance. Local npm release gate exited 1 at 297 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped out of 304; measured index.ts coverage 97.91/93.98/98.51 meets unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. All seven existing ambiguity tests fail only whole-tracker byte comparison after source-harness refusal: added fingerprint caches and rewritten aliases under runtime/metadata-cache, no item or input differences in the reported hunks. Artifact lifecycle regressions passed. Search found only the closed fidelity owner cache-priming note; new follow-up pm-todos-cache-context under that owner tracks CLI-versus-SDK fixture/cache isolation. No core source edit or upstream issue filing. Bun and isolated-HOME full gates remain active; do not treat CI passes as those local results."
  "2026-10-11T07:25:40.429Z",codex-agent,"Isolated-HOME full release check on unchanged bb33acd with Node 22.18.0/npm 10.9.3 exited 0: 304/304 tests, no skips, coverage inventory one configured source and unchanged thresholds met; canonical-reader acceptance 1/1; production audit zero vulnerabilities; packed matrix 4/4 (npm and Bun, host 2026.10.6 and minimum 2026.8.20), each imported one and exported two real fixtures; changelog/date/provenance gates passed. Runtime and environment differ from the regular local Node 24 gate, so cache-context cause remains a separate investigation. Bun full gate is still running; queued duplicate identity run will be stopped after Bun completes because the independent full identity result is now complete."
  "2026-10-11T07:42:18.253Z",codex-agent,"Final validation on unchanged artifact-guard source: npm run release:check exit 1 and bun run release:check exit 1, each 304 tests / 297 passed / 7 failed / 0 skipped, all failures existing ambiguity snapshots differing only in SDK-owned runtime metadata-cache files. Independent env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check with Node 22.18.0/npm 10.9.3 exited 0: 304/304, canonical-reader 1/1, packed npm/Bun current/minimum matrix 4/4, zero production vulnerabilities and changelog/date/attestation passed. Queued duplicate identity attempt was stopped after both regular gates completed; it is not counted as validation. CI run 38118503344 passes 304/304 on Node 22.18 and Node 26. Lifecycle and PM-linked tests passed 11/11; function-only artifact predicate revert produced two loaded lock assertion failures, restoration passed 3/3; npm 10 real-pack scratch proof failed 1 assertion on function-only revert and passed 1/1 restored. Source and pinned installer suffix are intact. Follow-ups pm-todos-7bk6 and pm-todos-cache-context remain open; PR #117 remains draft with failed local gates and missing final-head review. Release PR #116 is unchanged and must be closed and regenerated after this fix merges. Final PM release, changelog generation/check and paired history verification follow; no item is closed."
  "2026-10-11T10:20:29.769Z",claude-hub,"Review fix: the real-pack regression now runs npm's genuine prepare lifecycle (no --ignore-scripts) and asserts the guard saw npm_command=pack. Revert proof: guard predicate forced false -> test fails 0/1; restored passes 1/1. Isolated release:check 304/304."
